<body>
<h1>A6 — HTTP RAG (POST /ask_batched)</h1>
<p>A5 answers from the terminal (<code>scripts/ask_rag.py</code>). A6 is the same function behind FastAPI. The client sends JSON; the server loads <code>data/embeddings.json</code>, retrieves chunks, asks the chat model, saves a SQLite row, and returns JSON.</p>
<p><code>POST /ask</code> is still a plain text stream. It does not search the corpus.</p>
<p><b>Related files:</b> <code>src/api/main.py</code>, <code>src/rag/ask_rag.py</code>, <code>src/rag/retrieve.py</code>, <code>data/embeddings.json</code>, <code>tests/test_api.py</code>.</p>

<h2>What the live call did</h2>
<p>Server already running on port 8000. Index: 3 chunks from <code>leave_policy</code>, dim 1536.</p>
<pre>curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/ask_batched \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"question":"How many annual leave days does Northstar grant?"}'</pre>
<p>Response:</p>
<pre>{
  "content": "Northstar Labs grants annual leave based on years of continuous service: employees with 0 to 2 years of service receive 18 working days, those with 2 to 5 years receive 22 working days, and employees with 5 or more years receive 25 working days per calendar year. Part-time staff receive a pro-rata entitlement based on their contracted hours.",
  "cost_usd": 0.00012495,
  "retries": 0,
  "confidence": 1.0,
  "sources": ["leave_policy#0", "leave_policy#2", "leave_policy#1"],
  "schema_version": "v1"
}</pre>

<h2>Steps inside that one HTTP request</h2>
<table>
<tr><th>Step</th><th>What happens</th></tr>
<tr><td>1. Body</td><td>FastAPI reads <code>question</code>. Empty string → HTTP 422.</td></tr>
<tr><td>2. Index</td><td>Read <code>data/embeddings.json</code>. Missing file → HTTP 503. This run had 3 rows.</td></tr>
<tr><td>3. Embed</td><td><code>text-embedding-3-small</code> via Vocareum <code>/embeddings</code>. One 1536-d vector.</td></tr>
<tr><td>4. Rank</td><td>NumPy cosine. Order: <code>leave_policy#0</code> (the 18/22/25 table), then #2, then #1.</td></tr>
<tr><td>5. Chat</td><td><code>gpt-4o-mini</code> at <code>/chat/completions</code>. Prompt is those three chunks plus the question. Answer only from that context.</td></tr>
<tr><td>6. sources</td><td>The JSON <code>sources</code> are the retrieved chunk ids, in score order.</td></tr>
<tr><td>7. Save</td><td>One row in <code>data/answers.db</code>.</td></tr>
<tr><td>8. Reply</td><td>HTTP 200 with the fields above. This run cost about $0.000125.</td></tr>
</table>
<p>The answer matches the policy: 18 days (0–2 years), 22 (2–5), 25 (5+), plus pro-rata for part-time. That sentence is in <code>leave_policy#0</code>, which is why it ranked first.</p>

<h2>A5 vs A6</h2>
<table>
<tr><th></th><th>A5</th><th>A6</th></tr>
<tr><td>How you call it</td><td><code>python scripts/ask_rag.py "…"</code></td><td><code>curl POST /ask_batched</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Search and model</td><td>Same <code>ask_rag</code></td><td>Same <code>ask_rag</code></td></tr>
<tr><td>Result</td><td>Printed in the terminal</td><td>JSON over HTTP, also saved in SQLite</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>Start the server</h2>
<pre>source .venv/bin/activate
python scripts/build_index.py
uvicorn src.api.main:app --reload --port 8000</pre>
<p><code>USE_FAKE=true</code> only works if the JSON file was also built with fake 8-d vectors. The real index is 1536-d, so leave <code>USE_FAKE=false</code>.</p>
<p>Interactive docs while the server runs: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs</p>

<h2>Tests (no Vocareum)</h2>
<pre>pytest tests/test_api.py -q</pre>
<p>These inject a tiny index and a fake answer. They check that <code>/ask_batched</code> returns chunk ids in <code>sources</code> and that a missing index is 503.</p>
</body>
</html>
